 "explanation": "LangChain hashes page_content + metadata; with the source in metadata identical chunk texts in different documents get different record keys, so index() deduplicates per document and per batch (distinct keys): it matches S1-distinct, not the global S2 scope. With start_index, any length change before a chunk changes its metadata hash and forces a re-embedding. With the default batch_size=100, incremental cleanup runs after every batch and deletes the source's records not yet seen in this run, so a document with more than 100 chunks re-embeds its later batches on every update; with batch_size=10000 the counts equal S1-distinct.",
